'\" t
.TH ARO 5 2026-09-27 "aro 0.4.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
aro \- configuration file for the aro Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aro/config
.RI ( ~/.config/aro/config )
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file is a list of
.I key
.B =
.I value
lines.
Everything after
.B #
is a comment, and every key is optional: aro works with no file at all.
Keys are case-insensitive.
A value may be wrapped in single or double quotes, which is how names
with spaces are written:
.BR "cursor_theme = 'Some Theme'" .
.PP
Saving the file applies it immediately.
A line that cannot be read is skipped and reported on screen with its line
number; the rest of the file still applies.
.B aro \-c
checks a file without starting aro.
.PP
Values are written as:
.TP
.I bool
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off ,
.BR 1 / 0 .
.TP
.I colour
.BR 0x RRGGBBAA,
.BR # RRGGBBAA
or RRGGBBAA; the alpha pair is optional and defaults to ff.
.TP
.I ms
A duration in milliseconds.
.SH GENERAL
.TP
.BR mod " = " super | alt
The modifier that
.B mod
means in bindings.
Default: super.
Use alt when running nested.
.TP
.BI "focus_follows_mouse = " bool
Focus the window under the pointer.
Default: false.
.TP
.BI "confirm_quit = " bool
Ask before the quit binding ends the session.
Default: true.
.TP
.BI "allow_tearing = " bool
Let a fullscreen app that asks for it, usually a game, show each frame at
once instead of waiting for the screen's refresh.
Input lag drops, at the cost of visible tearing.
Only that app is affected, and only while it is fullscreen.
Default: false.
.TP
.BR layout " = " manual | dwindle | monocle | scroll
How new windows are placed.
.B manual
splits beside the focused window, the way
.B mod+v
and
.B mod+s
last said;
.B dwindle
splits along the longer side, so the layout spirals;
.B monocle
shows one window at a time, filling the screen, with the splits kept
underneath for when you leave it;
.B scroll
puts windows in columns on an endless strip that the screen scrolls
along, following focus, with the neighbouring columns peeking in at the
edges.
A window opened or dropped beside another starts a new column; one opened
below it
.RB ( mod+s )
or dropped above or below it shares that column.
Default: manual.
.TP
.BI "scroll_width = " share
How wide a new column is in the scroll layout, from 0.1 to 1.0 of the
screen.
.B mod+ctrl+h
and
.B mod+ctrl+l
change the focused column's width.
Default: 0.5.
.TP
.BI "scroll_presets = " "share ..."
The widths
.B width
steps a column through, up to eight.
Default: 0.333 0.5 0.667.
.TP
.BI "scroll_peek = " pixels
How much of the neighbouring columns stays visible at the screen's edges
in the scroll layout; 0 shows whole columns only.
Default: 40.
.TP
.BI "workspace = " "n " layout " name"
The layout of workspace
.IR n ,
1 to 32, overriding
.BR layout .
.B mod+t
changes it for the current workspace until the next config change.
.TP
.BI "workspaces = " n
How many workspaces the bar, and bars using ext-workspace, show even when
empty: 1 to 32.
Default: 4.
More appear as you use them.
.TP
.BR header " = " always | auto
.B always
draws aro's title header on every window;
.B auto
leaves it out for windows that draw their own.
Default: always.
.TP
.BR workspace_slide " = " horizontal | vertical | off
How switching workspaces moves.
Default: horizontal.
.SH INPUT
.TP
.BR keyboard_layout ", " keyboard_variant ", " keyboard_options ", " keyboard_model ", " keyboard_rules
The XKB settings, for example
.B keyboard_layout = us,br
and
.BR "keyboard_options = compose:ralt" .
Unset ones come from the
.B XKB_DEFAULT_*
environment variables.
.TP
.BI "keyboard_repeat_rate = " n
Keys per second while a key is held; 0 turns repeat off.
Default: 25.
.TP
.BI "keyboard_repeat_delay = " ms
How long a key is held before it repeats.
Default: 600.
.TP
.BI "touchpad_tap = " bool
Tap to click.
Default: true.
.TP
.BI "touchpad_natural_scroll = " bool
Default: false.
.TP
.BI "touchpad_disable_while_typing = " bool
Default: true.
.TP
.BI "touchpad_speed = " number
From \-1.0 to 1.0.
Default: 0.
.TP
.BI "mouse_accel = " "auto | flat | adaptive"
The acceleration profile for mice and trackpoints.
.B flat
moves the pointer by the same amount however fast the mouse goes.
Default: auto, the device's own default.
.TP
.BI "mouse_speed = " number
From \-1.0 to 1.0.
Default: 0.
.TP
.BI "mouse_natural_scroll = " bool
Default: false.
.TP
.BI "lid_switch = " bool
Closing a laptop's lid turns its built-in screen off while another screen is
on, and opening it turns it back on.
With no other screen the lid is left to the system (logind), which usually
suspends.
Default: true.
.TP
.BI "gesture_fingers = " n
A touchpad swipe with this many fingers, 3 to 5, changes workspace on the
screen under the pointer when the fingers lift: to the left for the next
one, to the right for the previous, or up and down with
.BR "workspace_slide = vertical" .
Then a sideways swipe on a
.B scroll
workspace moves focus to the next or previous column.
0 leaves every gesture to apps.
Other gestures, such as pinching, always go to the app under the pointer.
Default: 3.
.TP
.BI "cursor_theme = " name
The cursor theme; a theme that cannot be found is reported.
Default:
.BR $XCURSOR_THEME ,
or the system default.
Programs started afterwards get it through
.BR XCURSOR_THEME ;
GTK programs read the gsettings key
.B org.gnome.desktop.interface cursor-theme
instead.
.TP
.BI "cursor_size = " n
From 8 to 256.
Default:
.BR $XCURSOR_SIZE ,
or 24.
.SH MONITORS
A block configures every screen whose connector name (such as
.BR HDMI-A-1 )
or "make model serial" description matches a glob.
aro logs both when a screen appears.
Blocks that match all apply, later ones winning.
.PP
.nf
monitor HDMI-A-1 {
    mode = 2560x1440@144
    position = 1920,0
    scale = auto
}
.fi
.TP
.BR enabled " = " \fIbool\fP | auto
Default: on.
aro will not turn off its only screen.
.TP
.BR mode " = " \fIW\fP x \fIH\fP [ @\fIHz\fP "] | " auto
A resolution, with an optional refresh rate; the closest rate is used.
.B auto
is the screen's preferred mode.
.TP
.BR position " = " \fIX\fP , \fIY\fP " | " auto
In layout pixels, after scaling.
.B auto
places it to the right of the others.
.TP
.BR scale " = " \fInumber\fP " | " auto
From 0 to 10;
.B auto
is 2 above 192 DPI, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.BR transform " = " normal | 90 | 180 | 270 | flipped | flipped-90 | flipped-180 | flipped-270 | auto
Rotation.
.TP
.BR adaptive_sync " = " \fIbool\fP | auto
Variable refresh rate.
Default: off.
.TP
.BR hdr " = " \fIbool\fP | auto
Drive an HDR monitor in HDR, ten bits a channel.
It needs a renderer that converts colours, which today is only
.B WLR_RENDERER=vulkan
in a build without effects; otherwise, and on a monitor that does not
report HDR, the screen stays as it is and the log says why.
That renderer also lets apps tell aro what colours they draw in.
Default: off.
.PP
A key left out keeps whatever the screen has, so changes made with tools
such as wlr-randr survive a reload;
.B auto
resets it.
.SH BAR AND WALLPAPER
.TP
.BR bar " = " auto | true | false
.B auto
hides aro's bar on a screen where another bar, such as waybar, reserves
space, and brings it back half a second after that bar goes.
.B true
always shows it,
.B false
never.
Default: auto.
.TP
.BI "bar_battery = " bool
The battery's charge left of the clock, when the machine has one;
.B charging
while it is, and in the urgent colour at 15% and below.
Default: true.
.TP
.BR wallpaper " = " auto | none | \fIpath\fP
.B auto
is aro's own wallpaper;
.B none
leaves the background to you;
a path shows that image (PNG, JPEG, WebP, SVG with librsvg), covering the
screen.
.B ~
is expanded.
aro runs
.BR aropaper (1)
for it.
.BR "aropaper " \fIfile\fP
or
.B aroctl wallpaper
changes it without this line, and aro remembers that in
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/aro/wallpaper
across sessions, until this line changes.
So does the picker the
.B wallpapers
action opens.
Default: auto.
.TP
.BI "wallpaper_dir = " path
A folder for the wallpaper picker to list, with the folders inside it,
three levels deep.
Repeat the line for more; each adds one.
aro's own wallpapers are always listed, one entry per wallpaper whatever
the sizes it comes in.
With no
.B wallpaper_dir
line,
.I ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
(or
.I ~/Pictures
when there is none) and
.IR ~/.local/share/backgrounds .
.B ~
is expanded.
Thumbnails are made by
.BR aropaper (1)
and kept in
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/aro/thumbnails .
.SH LOOK
.TS
